From 8fdd60096e6b5b2fad7993864c65ae527058e71d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WWE13 Recomp <wwe13-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:08:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 118/118] ios: map guest views where iOS allows; window size
 and orientation

Follow-up to the iOS build patch, from testing rex_smoke on an iPad mini
(iPadOS, arm64, 12 GB):

- Memory::Initialize: iOS refused every fixed base it tried
  (1<<32 .. 1<<40: the low ones hold the app and the shared cache, the
  high ones are beyond the app's address space), so Initialize failed
  even with the Mach memory entry. On iOS it now reserves the guest span
  plus 4 GB anywhere, takes the 4 GB-aligned base inside, releases the
  reservation and maps the views there; the fixed bases stay as the
  fallback. With it: guest memory reserve/access and MMIO read/write
  traps PASS on the iPad.
- Window size: with a Metal view, SDL_GetWindowSizeInPixels reports the
  layer's drawableSize on iOS, which keeps the old orientation after a
  rotation; window size, surface size and touch scaling now use points
  x pixel density (GetSDLWindowPixelSize).
- Orientation: SDL's view controller settled on portrait; force
  landscape (SDL_HINT_ORIENTATIONS), as the app's Info.plist says.
- rex_smoke shows a build stamp, to tell builds apart on a device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
